00:52:52.430 --> 00:52:56.300
So I do believe that
LaTeX is an option,

00:52:56.300 --> 00:52:57.510
but hasn't been implemented.

00:52:57.510 --> 00:53:01.420
I possibly need to hand it
over to Charlotta to confirm.

00:53:01.420 --> 00:53:04.130
But we would be looking
at different engines,

00:53:04.130 --> 00:53:06.172
too, for reporting.

00:53:06.172 --> 00:53:07.380
CHARLOTTA FRUCHTENICHT: Yeah.

00:53:07.380 --> 00:53:10.050
Just to add to that,
actually, and I

00:53:10.050 --> 00:53:13.670
saw there was another question
on the chat about gt summary.

00:53:13.670 --> 00:53:17.340
So the reason why we build
our own table rendering

00:53:17.340 --> 00:53:21.210
was to support different
engines, namely kable, GT

00:53:21.210 --> 00:53:22.460
and DT.

00:53:22.460 --> 00:53:25.590
And that is specifically because
some of these already come

00:53:25.590 --> 00:53:27.210
with LaTeX support.

00:53:27.210 --> 00:53:29.520
And that is implemented
already, at least

00:53:29.520 --> 00:53:32.040
in the rudimentary form.

00:53:32.040 --> 00:53:34.410
Regarding templates, I
think that's a great idea.

00:53:34.410 --> 00:53:37.890
We haven't really-- we haven't
really reached that stage yet.

00:53:37.890 --> 00:53:42.030
But we try to
create the functions

00:53:42.030 --> 00:53:43.680
at the moment in the
flexible way that

00:53:43.680 --> 00:53:47.730
allows easy integration in
different markdown output

00:53:47.730 --> 00:53:49.560
formats, as well as Shiny.

00:53:52.080 --> 00:53:54.330
MARC VANDEMEULEBROECKE: Thank
you, Mark and Charlotta.

00:53:57.690 --> 00:53:59.650
Here's a question.

00:53:59.650 --> 00:54:02.440
Is it plans to have
only survival analysis

00:54:02.440 --> 00:54:04.930
or other epidemiological
model or analysis?

00:54:04.930 --> 00:54:06.910
I think the answer
is clearly yes,

00:54:06.910 --> 00:54:12.070
we want to expand to many
different types of analysis.

00:54:12.070 --> 00:54:15.790
Common ones and gradually
perhaps a little less

00:54:15.790 --> 00:54:17.080
common ones as well.

00:54:20.280 --> 00:54:23.280
One question I think is
important here just coming in.

00:54:23.280 --> 00:54:25.350
What level of
proficiency are you

00:54:25.350 --> 00:54:29.620
looking for in contributors?

00:54:29.620 --> 00:54:34.032
Maybe Charlotta, do you
want to answer this one?

00:54:34.032 --> 00:54:35.240
CHARLOTTA FRUCHTENICHT: Sure.

00:54:35.240 --> 00:54:39.680
I guess we are open for
all levels of proficiency.

00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:43.640
So as we said, this package
is at a really early stage.

00:54:43.640 --> 00:54:49.280
So we'd love to hear and
see people contribute

00:54:49.280 --> 00:54:51.890
who have a lot of experience
in developing R packages,

00:54:51.890 --> 00:54:54.380
from which we could
probably learn quite a bit,

00:54:54.380 --> 00:54:57.230
being more on the data
sides and domain expert side

00:54:57.230 --> 00:54:58.310
at the moment.

00:54:58.310 --> 00:55:01.940
But then also people who
come in who would be, like,

00:55:01.940 --> 00:55:06.080
target users or who want
to write documentation

00:55:06.080 --> 00:55:08.240
or vignettes are very welcome.

00:55:08.240 --> 00:55:10.940
So all levels of proficiency
are welcome to join the team.

00:55:12.567 --> 00:55:14.400
MARC VANDEMEULEBROECKE:
Thank you very much.

00:55:14.400 --> 00:55:16.560
And maybe a last
question, because we only

00:55:16.560 --> 00:55:17.700
have one minute left.

00:55:17.700 --> 00:55:21.060
Someone has asked
about the possibility

00:55:21.060 --> 00:55:25.410
to incorporate
corporate branding color

00:55:25.410 --> 00:55:30.210
schemes and the like on top of
the good graphical principles.

00:55:30.210 --> 00:55:31.560
The answer is clearly yes.

00:55:31.560 --> 00:55:33.840
That's the way the
package is designed.

00:55:36.840 --> 00:55:41.100
It should be possible
to plug your personal,

00:55:41.100 --> 00:55:43.950
or your company's
corporate branding,

00:55:43.950 --> 00:55:49.320
at the very last step on
top of the visualizations.

00:55:49.320 --> 00:55:52.670
[MUSICAL STRUM]

